These are role targets, not additional Effect permissions. Discover, healing and other supplementary purchases in a conflict follow the action or explicit ability that permits them (Core Rules §5, §10.6); the complete supplementary permission list remains an open ruling.

=== 9.2 Things to Watch in Playtest
- #strong[Discount stacking:] abilities that reduce Power costs (Silver Tongue, Analyze, Field Medic, Deadly Precision, Jury-Rig) can be strong with Effort for Power. Follow their stated scopes. For Create, each explicit discount reduces the cost by 1 Power to a minimum of 1 (Core Rules §5); these notes impose no blanket one-discount-per-Effect cap. Restore-cost discounts do not lift the ordinary 1-tier lasting-injury treatment limit (§6.6). Any further stacking cap is a separate balance proposal, not a rule introduced here.
- #strong[Free bonus dice] (Berserker, Animal Companion, Second Wind, Nobody Sees Me Coming) still count toward the +2 bonus die maximum. Free benefits grant no extra scripted turn or rotation bypass.
- #strong[Adept workings] are the most open-ended. If they overshadow other playbooks, playtest increasing the base working cost to 2 pool points or letting Focused Channel apply only to minor and significant workings. These are proposals, not changes to the printed abilities.
- #strong[Vehicle signature items] (Explorator, modern and sci-fi) are 0 load because they don\'t come on foot missions. A recorded vehicle can matter as a story fact, but its action benefit requires relevant use or an established contribution; an absent vehicle gives no automatic bonus (Core Rules §10.10).
- #strong[Refresh accounting:] a ★ Major costs 1 Refresh when taken; as a creation extra it also pays that extra ability's 1 Refresh, for 2 total. Veteran costs remain additional. Actual remaining Refresh depends on the acquisition route and other purchases, not simply the number of ★ abilities. A capstone costs no Refresh but retains its prerequisites (Playbook Rules §1.2).
- #strong[Conflict separation:] watch additional Power, Disposition loss and status-tier bonuses separately. Do not apply one bonus to both loss and harm unless stated. Companions that act independently enter continuous rotation; supporting assets do not gain independent turns merely by supplying a tag (Core Rules §10.6, §10.9).
